  "schoolyard_use_notes": "This tree has glossy, dark green leaves that are aromatic when crushed, making it useful for lessons on plant scents and essential oils. Its small, yellowish flowers bloom in clusters, attracting pollinators and providing a real-life example of plant-pollinator interactions. The tree's evergreen nature allows for year-round study of leaf structure and function. Its dense foliage can also serve as a living backdrop for outdoor classroom activities.",
